# TODO - ROCm adapter contract reservation

## Objective

Reserve a hardware-neutral ROCm adapter identity and capability boundary without
implementing, packaging, benchmarking, or advertising ROCm support until
supported AMD hardware and an explicit maintainer are available.

## Acceptance

- Shared compiler, optimizer, verifier, bootstrap, and CLI code contains no ROCm
  package, HIP runtime, AMD driver, or device requirement.
- Selecting the reserved adapter reports a stable unavailable/not-implemented
  diagnostic and may fall back to the CPU/reference path only where the caller
  explicitly permits accelerator fallback.
- No ROCm dependency is installed by the public bootstrap, no fake device
  evidence is committed, and this reservation does not block the turnkey
  C-to-Malbolge completion gate.
- The hardware-neutral accelerator port remains sufficient for a future real
  adapter without introducing CUDA-specific types into shared contracts.

## Evidence

- Required evidence is limited to the reviewed contract, stable unavailable
  diagnostic, and proof that CPU and CUDA paths do not depend on ROCm packages.
- A future implementation requires a new reviewed TODO with supported AMD
  hardware, exact ROCm/OS identity, differential tests, and retained live-device
  evidence.
